  "summary": "Suffolk County, NY legislators grilled Flock Safety representatives for over two hours on October 8, 2026 about the county's ~200 license-plate cameras and $5 million contract, pressing on 30-day data retention, access controls, Fourth Amendment concerns, and a recent Oklahoma federal ruling. Lawmakers signaled plans to draft a local law regulating police searches of Flock data and holding Flock liable, while the camera network remains in place.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Suffolk County legislators spent more than two hours grilling Flock Safety representatives on October 8th over the company's network of roughly 200 license-plate-reading cameras scattered across the county",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "99% of courts upheld Jim Crow laws for 56 years",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Legislator Greg Doroski said the legislature is working with the county police department on a strict local law to regulate police searches of Flock data, one that would make Flock Safety liable under its terms",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "More than 50 agencies or communities have canceled, suspended or rejected a Flock contract or deactivated their cameras since the beginning of 2026",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
